  "question": {
    "text": "A round uniform body of radius $\\mathrm{R}$, mass $\\mathrm{M}$ and moment of inertia '$\\mathrm{I}$', rolls down (without slipping) an inclined plane making an angle $\\theta$ with the horizontal. Then its acceleration is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\mathrm{g} \\sin \\theta}{1+\\frac{\\mathrm{I}}{\\mathrm{M R}^2}}$\n",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\mathrm{g} \\sin \\theta}{1+\\frac{\\mathrm{M R}^2}{\\mathrm{I}}}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\mathrm{g} \\sin \\theta}{1-\\frac{\\mathrm{I}}{\\mathrm{MR}^2}}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\mathrm{g} \\sin \\theta}{1-\\frac{\\mathrm{M R}^2}{\\mathrm{I}}}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{M g \\sin \\theta-f=M a}$\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\mathrm{f R=I \\frac{a}{R}}\\\\\n& \\Rightarrow a=\\frac{g \\sin \\theta}{\\left(1+\\frac{\\mathrm{I}}{\\mathrm{M}\\mathrm{R^2}}\\right)}\n\\end{aligned}$\n<img src=\"assets\\st0252_7cb96f80c5ee.png\"><br>"
  }
